    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Integrate matrix block processing, AVX2 vectorization, and OpenMP parallelism to improve performance while fixing compilation errors and ensuring correctness.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Reorganize the matrix processing into blocks\",\n    \"Adjust loop orders for better cache performance\",\n    \"Include immintrin.h conditionally based on compiler support\",\n    \"Adjust vectorized operations to handle cases where s is not a multiple of 8 without causing out-of-bounds access\",\n    \"Add OpenMP parallel for directive to parallelize the initial sum calculation of the first SxS submatrix\",\n    \"Use OpenMP reduction clause to handle the mxSum variable in a thread-safe manner\",\n    \"Adjust the loop scheduling to dynamic to better distribute work among threads\"\n  ],\n  \"sources_kept\": [\n    \"36575c0b38564080\",\n    \"976c4e4a29864704\",\n    \"bcdb340e8104428e\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#ifdef __AVX2__\\n#include <immintrin.h>\\n#endif\\n#include <omp.h>\\n#include <climits>\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n, s;\\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) \\n            scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n    assert(s < n);\\n    assert(n < 8000);\\n    assert(s > 0);\\n    assert(n > 0);\\n\\n    const int blockSize = 32; // Define a block size for better cache performance\\n    int mxSum = INT_MIN;\\n\\n    #pragma omp parallel reduction(max:mxSum)\\n    {\\n        int local_mxSum = INT_MIN;\\n        for (int bi = 0; bi <= n - s; bi += blockSize) {\\n            for (int bj = 0; bj <= n - s; bj += blockSize) {\\n                int sum = 0;\\n                for (int i = bi; i < std::min(bi + blockSize, n - s + 1); ++i) {\\n                    for (int j = bj; j < std::min(bj + blockSize, n - s + 1); ++j) {\\n                        sum = 0;\\n                        for (int ii = i; ii < i + s; ++ii) {\\n                            for (int jj = j; jj < j + s; ++jj) {\\n#ifdef __AVX2__\\n                                if (s % 8 == 0) {\\n                                    __m256i sum_vec = _mm256_setzero_si256();\\n                                    for (int k = 0; k < s; k += 8) {\\n                                        sum_vec = _mm256_add_epi32(sum_vec, _mm256_loadu_si256((__m256i*)&matrix[ii][jj + k]));\\n                                    }\\n                                    int temp_sum[8];\\n                                    _mm256_storeu_si256((__m256i*)temp_sum, sum_vec);\\n                                    for (int k = 0; k < 8; k++) {\\n                                        sum += temp_sum[k];\\n                                    }\\n                                } else {\\n#endif\\n                                    sum += matrix[ii][jj];\\n#ifdef __AVX2__\\n                                }\\n#endif\\n                            }\\n                        }\\n                        local_mxSum = std::max(local_mxSum, sum);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        #pragma omp critical\\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum, local_mxSum);\\n    }\\n    printf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"This integration combines matrix block processing for better cache performance, AVX2 vectorization for faster summation when s is a multiple of 8, and OpenMP parallelism to distribute the workload across threads. The reduction clause ensures that the mxSum variable is updated in a thread-safe manner.\"\n}"
